        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(slack): allow configurable App Home views",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSlack operators cannot customize the App Home tab without patching installed package files. OpenClaw republishes its built-in Home view whenever a workspace member opens the tab.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds one deliberately narrow config surface: `channels.slack.appHome.view` (with account-level override support).\n\n- The view is inline-only; there is no event-time filesystem `viewPath` contract.\n- Config changes follow the normal OpenClaw config reload/account lifecycle.\n- The runtime accepts `type: \"home\"` or fills it when omitted, requires 1-100 block objects, and preserves forward compatibility with new Slack block types.\n- Invalid local config is logged and falls back to the built-in safe view.\n- If Slack rejects the custom view at `views.publish`, the error cause is logged and the built-in view is published as a fallback.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can provide workspace-specific onboarding/help content in the Slack Home tab without editing generated or installed files. Existing installations with no `appHome` config keep the current built-in behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent contributor head: `666f4dba349` on upstream `main` `e5b2ca3c6bd`.\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/monitor/events/home.test.ts extensions/slack/src/config-schema.test.ts`: 46/46 passed.\n- Positive coverage: inline custom view, omitted `type`, account override, slash-command hint, and 100-block Home payload.\n- Negative/fallback coverage: invalid envelope/block shapes, more than 100 blocks, Slack API rejection, mismatched app events, and Messages-tab events.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check` passed.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --check` passed.\n- Direct formatter check and `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- The pre-PR plan gate passed for core, extension, test, config, and docs lanes with no dependency-sensitive changes.\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nThe focused handler tests exercise the real config merge, Home-view normalization, Bolt event registration, `views.publish` call shape, API-rejection error path, and built-in fallback. They prove both successful custom publication and the closest availability failure in-process.\n\nNo private Slack test app/workspace was configured on this machine, so this exact head has not published to the live Slack API. No Gateway restart or production Slack config change was performed. A redacted private-workspace publish remains the outstanding live transport proof if maintainers require it.\n\nAI-assisted; reviewed and validated before submission.\n",
